findings.detail:
E-Waste (Management) Rules 2022, rule 12: makers and producers of PV modules, panels and cells must:
- register on the CPCB portal;
- store PV waste generated up to 2034-35 under CPCB guidelines;
- file annual returns until then;
- keep a separate inventory.

PV recyclers must meet CPCB material-recovery norms. PV is listed as category CEEW14 in Schedule I, and Schedules III and IV say recycling targets do not apply to PV waste. So panels earn no EPR certificates today. The value lies in collection logistics, safe storage, reuse testing, hand-off to registered recyclers, and chain-of-custody records that producers can show. KERC assumes a 25-year plant life, so bulk end-of-life is years away; near-term volume comes from breakage, failures and repowering.
